        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127754,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127755,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This lesion affects the trunk and extremities.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127756,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are multiple erythematous papules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127757,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This rare haemangioma shows no sex predilection. Examples occurring outside the setting of multicentric Castleman disease or POEMS syndrome are likely to in fact be papillary haemangioma (see <em>Differential diagnosis</em>, below) {18001423; 19077091; 18805868; 17927585}. A rare association with Erdheim&ndash;Chester disease has been reported {30563806}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127758,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glomeruloid haemangioma is generally considered to be a reactive process.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127759,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Raised serum levels of VEGF have been described in one study, suggesting that this may play in a role in the development of the vascular lesions {30563806}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127760,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127761,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is dermal proliferation of dilated vascular channels containing clusters of capillaries that resemble renal glomeruli. The endothelial cells often contain intracytoplasmic inclusions that give a positive PAS reaction; these inclusions may be immunoglobulins, enlarged lysosomes, or thanatosomes {2173428; 19614998; 8030771}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>Papillary haemangioma has a predilection for the head and neck and manifests as a single lesion consisting of dermal dilated channels lined by endothelial cells with frequent papillary projections and lacking glomeruloid architecture {18805868}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127762,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127763,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127764,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> dilated dermal vascular channels with intraluminal proliferation of small blood vessels mimicking renal glomeruli.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127765,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127766,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 251,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glomeruloid haemangioma is benign but tends to persist, paralleling underlying systemic disease.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:56:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]